{"id": 295, "stem": "<div class=\"relative w-full min-w-0 max-w-full self-stretch\" id=\"question-text\"><span><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><mark class=\"bg-transparent dark:text-neutral-100\" data-markjs=\"true\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">A</mark> 54-year-old man is admitted to the hospital following a high-speed motor vehicle collision.\u00a0 He is found to have long bone fractures of the right leg that require open reduction/internal fixation.\u00a0 After the patient's condition is stabilized, he is transferred to a skilled nursing facility for extended rehabilitation.\u00a0 During his stay, his right leg is immobilized for several weeks.\u00a0 Management is complicated by decreased nutritional intake due to adverse effects of opioid pain medications.\u00a0 Measurement of the thigh following removal of casting materials finds a 2-cm decrease in diameter.\u00a0 The underlying process responsible for this patient's change in body measurement is most likely to also occur in which of the following?\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b</p></span></div>", "options": [{"label": "A", "text": "Adrenal glands during prolonged glucocorticoid therapy"}, {"label": "B", "text": "Bronchial tissue after prolonged tobacco smoke exposure"}, {"label": "C", "text": "Endometrial tissue during estrogen replacement therapy"}, {"label": "D", "text": "Esophageal mucosa on repeated acid exposure"}, {"label": "E", "text": "Heart muscle during long-standing hypertension"}], "correctAnswer": "A", "explanation": "<div class=\"relative w-full min-w-0 max-w-full self-stretch\" id=\"question-explanation\"><span class=\"\"><div id=\"div_t94255\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><div class=\"group/triggerable\" data-is-open=\"false\"><div class=\"group/draggable\" data-is-draggable=\"true\" data-is-dragging=\"false\"><div class=\"group/resizable relative\" data-is-maximized=\"false\" data-is-resizable=\"true\" data-is-resizing=\"false\"><div class=\"relative max-w-full\"><div aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"pointer-events-none absolute left-0 top-0 bottom-0 w-8 z-10 transition-opacity duration-200 bg-gradient-to-r from-white dark:from-nbme-primary-dark-800 warm:from-egg-sour-50 to-transparent opacity-0\"></div><div aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"pointer-events-none absolute right-0 top-0 bottom-0 w-8 z-10 transition-opacity duration-200 bg-gradient-to-l from-white dark:from-nbme-primary-dark-800 warm:from-egg-sour-50 to-transparent opacity-0\"></div><div class=\"max-w-full overflow-x-auto [&amp;_td]:min-w-[8rem] [&amp;_th]:min-w-[8rem]\"><table class=\"border bg-transparent dark:text-white border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white hover:bg-transparent warm:hover:bg-transparent dark:hover:bg-transparent cursor-default mt-2 mb-3\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><tbody style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" colspan=\"3\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><mark class=\"bg-transparent dark:text-neutral-50\" data-markjs=\"true\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">C</mark>ellular adaptations</strong></p></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Adaptation</strong></p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Definition</strong></p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Examples</strong></p></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Hyperplasia</strong></p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"width: 30%; font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">\u00a0\u2191 Cell number\u00a0\u2192 \u2191\u00a0organ size</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><ul class=\"flex flex-col justify-start items-start list-inside list-disc ml-4 mb-4\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Endometrial hyperplasia due to \u2191\u00a0estrogen</li><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Liver regeneration after partial hepatectomy</li></ul></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Hypertrophy</strong></p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">\u00a0\u2191 Cell size\u00a0\u2192 \u2191\u00a0organ size</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><ul class=\"flex flex-col justify-start items-start list-inside list-disc ml-4 mb-4\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Cardiac hypertrophy due to hypertension</li><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Uterine growth during pregnancy</li></ul></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Atrophy</strong></p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">\u2193 Cell size &amp; number\u00a0\u2192 \u2193\u00a0organ size</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><ul class=\"flex flex-col justify-start items-start list-inside list-disc ml-4 mb-4\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">\u2193 Skeletal muscle size from\u00a0immobilization</li><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">\u2193 Adrenal gland size due to glucocorticoid therapy</li></ul></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Metaplasia</strong></p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Replacement of 1 differentiated cell type with another</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><ul class=\"flex flex-col justify-start items-start list-inside list-disc ml-4 mb-4\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Bronchial squamous metaplasia due to tobacco smoke</li><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Esophageal intestinal metaplasia due to acid reflux</li></ul></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></div></div></div></div><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">This patient experienced a decreased physical workload when his leg was immobilized.\u00a0 As a result, the skeletal muscle fibers in the leg decreased in size, leading to disuse <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">atrophy</strong>.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><a class=\"hint\" data-exhibit-id=\"exhibit-syknkjwyfckqamtunj160c1p\" href=\"#exhibit-exhibit-syknkjwyfckqamtunj160c1p\">Atrophy</a> is <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">tissue loss</strong> due to <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">reduced cell size and number</strong> (ie, cellular death).\u00a0 It may be physiologic (eg, wolffian duct atrophy in the female fetus, maternal uterus atrophy following childbirth) or pathologic.\u00a0 Pathologic atrophy has a variety of causes, including lack of use, loss of hormonal or neurologic stimulation (denervation), impaired circulation, mechanical compression, aging, and nutritional insufficiency.\u00a0 On a cellular level, it represents an attempt to decrease the cell's metabolic requirements via a reduction in organelles (eg, mitochondria, rough endoplasmic reticulum) and protein synthesis, as well as an increase in protein breakdown.\u00a0 In prolonged atrophic states, irreversibly damaged cells may undergo <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">apoptosis</strong>, leading to reduced cellular numbers.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Pathologic atrophy also occurs in the <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">adrenal cortex</strong> during <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">prolonged glucocorticoid use</strong> due to suppression of <a class=\"hint\" data-exhibit-id=\"exhibit-hz5vxtmc94gyohn9fai7ulc9\" href=\"#exhibit-exhibit-hz5vxtmc94gyohn9fai7ulc9\">ACTH</a> release.\u00a0 For this reason, abrupt cessation of exogenous glucocorticoid therapy can lead to acute adrenal insufficiency and adrenal crisis.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">(Choice B)</strong>\u00a0 Prolonged exposure to tobacco smoke can induce metaplasia in the bronchial epithelium.\u00a0 This results in the normal columnar epithelium being replaced by squamous epithelium (ie, squamous metaplasia), causing an associated risk of squamous cell carcinoma.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">(Choice C)</strong>\u00a0 After menopause, falling estrogen levels can lead to atrophy of the breasts, endometrium, and vaginal mucosa.\u00a0 Conversely, estrogen replacement in these patients can cause endometrial hyperplasia (ie, increased cell number) unless combined with progesterone therapy.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">(Choice D)</strong>\u00a0 In chronic gastroesophageal reflux, esophageal mucosa subjected to repeated acid exposure may undergo metaplasia, in which the normal squamous epithelium is replaced by columnar epithelium with goblet cells (ie, Barrett esophagus).</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">(Choice E)</strong>\u00a0 Heart muscle subjected to long-standing hypertension is prone to developing hypertrophy (ie, increase in cell size), not atrophy.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Educational objective:</strong>Atrophy is a cellular adaptation characterized by a decrease in cell size and number, leading to decreased organ size.\u00a0 Pathologic atrophy has a variety of causes, including decreased physical workload, loss of innervation, decreased blood supply, inadequate nutrition, absent endocrine stimulation, aging, and mechanical pressure.\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b</p></span></div>", "educationalObjective": "Atrophy is a cellular adaptation characterized by a decrease in cell size and number, leading to decreased organ size.  Pathologic atrophy has a variety of causes, including decreased physical workload, loss of innervation, decreased blood supply, inadequate nutrition, absent endocrine stimulation, aging, and mechanical pressure.\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b", "subject": "Pathology", "system": "Miscellaneous (Multisystem)", "topic": "Cellular adaptation", "category": "Miscellaneous", "peerCorrect": 84.0}